##
    A project holding two programs and saying nothing about which one begins.

    These two are not the same name: one is Tools.Program and the other is App.Program, so
    nothing collides and both are perfectly good types. What is missing is the answer to a
    question the compiler must not answer for itself.

    It must not, because an assembly holds one entry point in its metadata. The choice is made
    when the thing is built, however it is spelled — and if the compiler picked, it would have
    to pick by the order the sources happen to be listed, which would make a build's behaviour
    depend on the order of its own file list. Swapping two lines here would change which
    program ran, and nothing would say so.

    The fix is one line: 'entry Tools.Program', or 'entry App.Program'. Written where there is
    only one program to begin with, that line decides nothing and is warned about instead.
##

project AmbiguousEntry
    source programs/Tools.pc
    source programs/App.pc
end project
